  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "The spoke directions, billow paths, ember drift and the scorch's rays and angle vary per cast. The 0.6 s gather, the throw at 600 ms, the 0.36 s flight and the blast at 1000 ms stay fixed so the hit lands at the same moment and the rune circle is a fair warning."
  },
  "director_notes": "A heavy fire blast for a top-down game. Choices: (1) a 0.6 s gather with a burning rune circle under the caster and a fireball swelling at the hand, so it reads as a big committed cast; (2) the fireball is lobbed (arc_height 70 px) so side and 3/4 views see a clear throw; (3) the payoff is a star: a dozen fast, long-streaked flame spokes (sparks at 900 px/s with streak_ms 130, no gravity) fired at once from the blast, over a screen flash, a fast shockwave, additive fireball billows, a dark plume and a wide scorch at detail 0.9 so its soot rays echo the star. The star is radial spokes, not a fixed glyph or letter shape, so every cast is different. Top is the hero view: the rune circle, the spokes, the ring and the rayed scorch carry it from above. Sound: fire while gathering, whoosh on the throw, boom plus rumble on the blast, quiet fire for the burnout."
}
